# Copy to ".env" in this folder (same directory as mcp.json):
#   copy .env.example .env
# Then set your GitHub fine-grained or classic PAT below (no quotes).
#
# The file ".cursor/.env" is gitignored. Cursor resolves ${env:GITHUB_PAT}
# in mcp.json from the environment Cursor inherited when it started, so you
# must expose this value to the app (pick one approach):
#
#   A) Windows: System Properties > Environment Variables > User > New
#      Name: GITHUB_PAT   Value: <your token>
#      Fully quit Cursor and reopen.
#
#   B) Launch Cursor from a shell where you already ran:
#      setx GITHUB_PAT "your_token_here"
#      (then restart the terminal / log off as needed for setx to apply)
#
#   C) If your setup loads a workspace .env into the editor process, ensure
#      GITHUB_PAT is defined there instead.
GITHUB_PAT=
